: "224370538", "author": {"steamid": "76561198103854927", "personaname": "Koftp", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/koftp/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 39, "playtime_forever": 1556, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 1329, "last_played": 1780179676, "avatar": "686bddf61cc248d0d02e99725225fbb84137f1c6"}, "language": "english", "review": "It's a decent game but it can only be played once\n\nI really like the card deck mechanic and the wound mechanic which makes you want to avoid taking damage and this game has a lot of potential for fun builds but the problem is the devs abandoned it. There will be no new updates, no new cards, no new maps, nothing.\n\nYou will be able to unlock most if not all unique cards throghout the campaign playthrough, or shortly after finishing all missions once, and it just leaves wishing for more. The replayability is not there, yeah, one can say \"erm, but you can build new decks with new weapons and new roles?\" but that still leaves you with the same levels, same enemies, same everything. I mean, it's just a grind with no goal in sight, unless you're an overachiever enjoying completing hardest difficulties just for your own amusement, it's just not it.\n\nIf Steam didn't have a binary review system, I'd give it a 7/10. Yeah, it's alright if you like L4D2 game genre and you have some friends you can pick the game up with when it's at -90% discount but there is no reason to get back to it later after finishing it once which is a bummer, I think devs stopped supporting it too early and it could've been much much better", "timestamp_created": 1777483412, "timestamp_updated": 1777483991, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 1, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": 0.5, "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1634050800", "hardware": {"system_